      "finding": "forwarder-cache-service-v2",
      "job": "consumer",
      "variants": [
        "probe",
        "negative"
      ],
      "diagnosis": "toolu never exports ACTIONS_CACHE_SERVICE_V2 or ACTIONS_CACHE_MODE in forwarder mode: execution::service_endpoints reads a job variable named ACTIONS_CACHE_SERVICE_V2, but GitHub sends actions_uses_cache_service_v2 = true and actions_cache_mode = write (see the committed compat_103_*_message.json captures). actions/cache therefore uses the retired v1 host artifactcache.actions.githubusercontent.com: `Save cache` logs the warning 'Failed to save: <h2>Our services aren't available right now</h2>' yet the step succeeds (no entry is created; GitHub's cache API lists only the official lane's keys), and the dependent `Restore cache` fails with 'Cache service responded with 400'. The official lane saves and restores.",
